      "independent_visual_review": "The exact former four-level full-rim mechanical tier pattern is gone. All 8 color and clay/silhouette angles show a solid slender irregular radial pillar with a modest coherent cap, broader eroded foot, three localized interrupted unequal ledges/asymmetric shoulders, and broken mineral bands that correspond to real relief. Top confirms irregular radial section; reverse/rear/clay/silhouette confirm ledges are not merely color patches or hidden by camera. Shape remains a generic cap-protected hoodoo teaching prop, not a named locality or measured stratigraphic section.",
